Build product features on shared foundations with clear ownership, predictable lifecycle behavior, and platform-appropriate implementations.

This guide covers six capabilities: **Design & Theming, Security & Credential Storage, Localization, Push Notifications, Branding, and Account Data Cleanup**. Each foundation defines its responsibilities, integration boundary, failure behavior, and implementation hints.

<Aside type="tip" title="Platform standard">
Use the approved foundation SDKs and generated resources. Product features consume semantic tokens and typed service contracts; they do not create their own credential stores, notification routers, or account-wipe routines. Android, iOS, and React Native share behavioral requirements while using their own platform APIs.
</Aside>

## Find the foundation you need

| Foundation | What it owns | What a feature provides |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Design & Theming | Semantic tokens, theme resolution, shared UI primitives | Accessible composition and product-specific layout |
| Security & Credential Storage | Credential access, key lifecycle, approved network security | Data classification and required access behavior |
| Localization | Translation resources, locale selection, formatting, layout direction | Translation keys, plural cases, and localizable content |
| Push Notifications | Registration, delivery adapters, validated routing | Supported destinations and authorization requirements |
| Branding | Approved brand registry, asset/token selection, platform icon adapters | An authorized brand selection and safe fallback |
| Account Data Cleanup | Access gating, stopped writers, scoped deletion, verification, recovery | A complete inventory of account-owned state and storage |

**Scope:** Examples illustrate foundation contracts and integration patterns. They are not a replacement for the SDK catalog's versioned installation instructions. Native setup, generated resources, application configuration, Redux registration, and service adapters must be supplied by the host application. Code here has not been compiled in your project.

