### Startup and session rules

1. Load validated local configuration and bundled theme/localization defaults.
2. Check for incomplete account cleanup before making protected data available.
3. Construct approved adapters with explicit process, scene, account, and screen lifetimes.
4. Resolve session readiness before rendering protected content or routing protected links.
5. Refresh remote configuration asynchronously where supported; retain safe local defaults.
6. Dispose subscriptions and cancel account work before replacing session-owned resources.

In React Native, use Redux Toolkit for shared preference and lifecycle state. Keep credentials, native SDK objects, functions, and subscription handles outside Redux state. RTK Query caches, when present, require their own account-reset handling.

